nts are modeled as guilds, not per-leaf geometry.\n./spec.md:593:- temperature\n./spec.md:615:Water temperature must be dynamic.\n./spec.md:620:dT/dt = (Q_ambient + Q_heater + Q_light - Q_evap) / heat_capacity\n./spec.md:626:- `Q_ambient` is based on temperature difference between ambient air and water and a geometry-dependent transfer coefficient\n./spec.md:635:Q_ambient = UA_total * (T_ambient - T_water)\n./spec.md:641:- small open tanks respond faster to ambient changes than large tanks\n./spec.md:642:- heaters partially buffer ambient swings\n./spec.md:643:- if ambient exceeds heater setpoint, heater cannot cool the tank\n./spec.md:644:- high ambient temperature reduces oxygen saturation and can stress shrimp\n./spec.md:662:- water changes\n./spec.md:666:- water changes\n./spec.md:670:- water changes\n./spec.md:674:Nitrification must be biomass-limited, oxygen-limited, temperature-sensitive, and pH-sensitive.\n./spec.md:702:- compute NH3 fraction from pH and temperature each tick\n./spec.md:745:- DO saturation decreases as temperature rises\n./spec.md:763:Then solve or approximate pH each tick from alkalinity + DIC + temperature.\n./spec.md:769:- do not hardcode pH as constant if plants, nitrification, and water changes occur\n./spec.md:790:- water temperature\n./spec.md:827:- temperature\n./spec.md:870:- temperature\n./spec.md:909:- temperature\n./spec.md:921:    f_temperature\n./spec.md:936:- temperature is stressful\n./spec.md:1003:- mixes in source water temperature and chemistry\n./spec.md:1014:### Change ambient temperature\n./spec.md:1015:- changes room environment, not instant water temperature\n./spec.md:1028:3. update water volume (evaporation/top-off/water change)\n./spec.md:1029:4. update temperature from ambient + heater + equipment\n./spec.md:1031:6. compute gas solubility targets from temperature\n./spec.md:1092:- warm ambient temperature reduced oxygen saturation\n./spec.md:1163:- save/load schema\n./spec.md:1257:- temperatures in °C\n./spec.md:1268:- no temperature below freezing in normal freshwater scenarios unless explicitly allowed\n./spec.md:1300:   - temperature\n./spec.md:1316:   - water change\n./spec.md:1319:   - change ambient temp\n./spec.md:1347:- 10 L tank must change temperature faster after ambient temp jump\n./spec.md:1349:## 20.4 Ambient temperature test\n./spec.md:1352:- ambient raised to 31 °C\n./spec.md:1378:At high sustained temperature, shrimp reproduction readiness and success must fall relative to moderate temperature conditions.\n./spec.md:1381:A large water change with very different GH/KH/TDS must improve some waste metrics while potentially increasing stress.\n./spec.md:1393:- save/load roundtrip test\n./spec.md:1395:## Milestone 1 — tank geometry and temperature\n./spec.md:1400:- temperature update system\n./spec.md:1401:- ambient temperature action\n./spec.md:1405:## Milestone 2 — dissolved pools and water changes\n./spec.md:1409:- water change/top-off actions\n./spec.md:1436:- high-temperature reproduction penalty\n./spec.md:1444:- save/load support\n./spec.md:1479:  - moderate temperature optimum\n./spec.md:1508:2. **ambient temperature as a real action**\n./spec.md:1509:3. **temperature-dependent water behavior**\n./spec.md:1510:4. **pH/temperature-dependent ammonia risk**\n./spec.md:1515:9. **deterministic save/load**\n./spec.md:1526:1. Ammonia speciation and toxicity depend strongly on pH and temperature.\n./spec.md:1530:5. Rising temperature interacts with nutrient regime and can shift aquatic plant performance and algal competition.\n./spec.md:1533:8. `Neocaridina davidi` reproduction is inhibited at sufficiently high sustained temperature.\n./spec.md:1542:2. Implement geometry derivation and unit tests.\n./spec.md:1544:4. Implement water change mixing.\n./spec.md:1545:5. Implement ambient temperature and heater tick.\n./spec.md:1565:- feed it, change water, and alter ambient temperature\n./spec.md:1580:- EPA CADDIS: **Ammonia** — ammonia occurs as NH3 + NH4+, higher pH