las: manual consumer printed expected values with zero diffs.\\n- [x] `PlayerAction` defines all 12 variants with typed validation errors: verified in [actions.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs), and invalid actions returned the expected `SimError` messages in manual testing.\\n- [x] `SimEvent`, `EventKind`, and `EventSeverity` are present with the required shapes: verified in [events.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/events.rs); manual consumer created `SimEvent`s successfully.\\n- [x] `SimSeed(u64)` wraps `ChaCha8Rng`, RNG is stored in `TankState`, and no thread-local RNG is used in `tank_core`: verified by `rg` and [rng.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/rng.rs) plus [state.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs).\\n- [x] `SimulationEngine` is implemented and actions are queued/processed at the next hourly tick in insertion order: manual output showed actions pending before `step_hours(1)` and applied after it; automated `action_queuing` also passed.\\n- [x] `TankState` contains the required top-level substates: verified in [state.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs).\\n- [x] Save file JSON contains schema version, app version, full `TankState`, queued actions, and RNG state: manual save/load run printed `has_schema=true ... has_rng=true` and restored state/queue equality.\\n- [x] `save_load_roundtrip` test exists and passes: confirmed by `cargo test`.\\n- [x] `determinism_basic` test exists and passes: confirmed by `cargo test`.\\n- [x] `action_validation` test exists and passes: confirmed by `cargo test`.\\n- [x] `action_queuing` test exists and passes: confirmed by `cargo test`.\\n- [x] Invariant checks run and enforce the required rules: manual run showed negative mass rejected, index-style values clamped into `0.0..=1.0`, and event log trimmed to 200; engine calls invariants from [engine.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs).\\n- [x] `tank_data` has TOML deserialization scaffolding and preset structs: manual preset loading succeeded; definitions are in [lib.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/lib.rs) and [presets.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs).\\n- [x] All required preset TOML files exist: verified with `find crates/tank_data/data -maxdepth 2 -type f`, which listed all source water, substrate, plant, shrimp, process, and scenario files.\\n- [x] `open_top = false` stores a configurable lid factor defaulting to `0.25`: manual geometry run printed `top_factor=0.250`; implementation is in [geometry.rs](/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/geometry.rs).\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/001-workspace-skeleton-core-types-rng-and-saveload/20260315031637-review-approved.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash -lc \\\"sed -n '1,260p' .ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops/001-workspace-skeleton-core-types-rng-and-saveload/20260315031637-review-approved.md\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"---\\nartifact: review-approved\\nloop: 1\\niterations: 0\\nproject: tank-sim\\nbackend: claude(opus)\\nrole: reviewer\\ncreated_at: 2026-03-15T03:16:37Z\\n---\\n\\nAll 4 tests pass. I've now reviewed every source file against the acceptance criteria. Let me write the review.\\n\\n# Review: APPROVED\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria Checklist\\n- [x] Cargo workspace compiles with four crates: `tank_core`, `tank_data`, `tank_tui`, `tank_scenarios`; `tank_core` has no TUI dependencies\\n- [x] `TankGeometry` struct defined with all 6 fields and all 7 derived calculations (`water_volume_l`, `surface_area_cm2`, `footprint_area_cm2`, `wall_area_cm2`, `mean_depth_cm`, `surface_area_to_volume_ratio`, `wall_area_to_volume_ratio`) using exact spec formulas\\n- [x] `WaterState` stores all required dissolved pools as total amounts (all nitrogen species, phosphate, DO, DIC, DOC, DON, alkalinity, and all 7 ion totals: Ca, Mg, Na, K, HCO3, Cl, SO4)\\n- [x] `TankSnapshot` derives all display values using exact spec formulas: `gh_d = ((2.497 * ca_mg_l) + (4.118 * mg_mg_l)) / 17.848`, `kh_d = (alkalinity_meq_l * 50.0) / 17.848`, `tds_mg_l = total_tracked_ions_mg / volume_l`, `conductivity_us_cm = tds_mg_l / 0.65`, pH from alkalinity/DIC with clamp to `[5.5, 8.5]`, NH3 speciation via `pKa = 0.09018 + 2729.92 / (273.2 + temp_c)`\\n- [x] `PlayerAction` enum with all 12 variants and validation returning typed `SimError` (percentages `0.0..=100.0`, fractions `0.0..=1.0`, non-negative grams, temperature > 0, non-empty source profile ID)\\n- [x] `SimEvent` struct with `day`, `hour`, `severity`, `kind`, `cause_codes`, `summary`; `EventKind` enum with all 13 required variants; `EventSeverity` with Info/Warning/Critical\\n- [x] `SimSeed(u64)` wraps `ChaCha8Rng` via `SimRng`; RNG stored in `TankState.rng`; no thread-local RNG in `tank_core`\\n- [x] `SimulationEngine` trait implemented on `Engine` with `apply_action`, `step_hours`, `snapshot`, `full_state`; actions queued in `VecDeque` and drained in insertion order at start of each hourly tick\\n- [x] `TankState` contains all top-level sub-states: geometry, environment, hardware (light/heater/filter/aeration), water, substrate layers, filter state, plant guild states, algae, microbe, microfauna, animal (shrimp), detritus, event log, RNG\\n- [x] Save file is JSON containing `schema_version`, `app_version`, full `TankState`, `queued_actions`, and serialized RNG state (seed + draw count)\\n- [x] `save_load_roundtrip` test: non-default seed (42), applies actions, steps 1 hour, serializes to JSON, deserializes, asserts field-by-field equality\\n- [x] `determinism_basic` test: two engines with same seed (7) stepping 24 hours produce identical snapshots and full state\\n- [x] `action_validation` test: negative grams → `NegativeValue`, percent 120 → `PercentOutOfRange`, fraction 1.1 → `FractionOutOfRange`, intensity -0.5 → `FractionOutOfRange`, intensity_index 1.2 → `FractionOutOfRange`, temperature 0.0 → `TemperatureTooLow`\\n- [x] `action_queuing` test: RemoveShrimp(1) then AddShrimp(1) on 0 adults → result is 1 (proves insertion-order processing since reversed order would yield 0)\\n- [x] Invariant checks run after every `step_hours`: non-negative mass pools, index values clamped `0.0..=1.0`, temperature > 0.0 C; event log trimmed to last 200\\n- [x] `tank_data` has TOML deserialization via `serde`/`toml` with preset structs for source water, substrate, plant, shrimp, process params, and scenarios; presets loaded via `include_str!` compile-time embedding\\n- [x] All preset TOML files created: source water (4), substrate (4), plants (2), shrimp (1), process params (1), scenarios (3) — all with `id`, `name`, parameters, and `[provenance]` blocks\\n- [x] `open_top = false` stores configurable `lid_exchange_factor` (default `0.25`) via `TankGeometry.lid_exchange_factor` with `top_exchange_factor()` returning the factor when closed\\n\\n## Notes\\n\\nSolid Milestone 1 implementation. A few observations (none blocking):\\n\\n- **RNG serialization strategy**: Seed + draw-count replay is correct but O(n) on deserialization. Acceptable for v1 draw counts; the debug assertion at 2^32 draws provides a safety net.\\n- **Water change dilution** correctly covers TAN, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC, DOC, DON, alkalinity, and all 7 ions — matching the future `water_change_mass_balance` test's required pools. DO is intentionally excluded (not required by that acceptance test).\\n- **Source water mixing** and **temperature mixing** during water changes are acknowledged as deferred to Milestone 2. `ChangeAmbientTemperature` correctly sets `environment.ambient_temp_c` (not water temp), ready for the heat model.\\n- Code is well-organized, consistently formatted, and `cargo test` passes cleanly across all 4 crates.\\n\\n## Commit Message\\n\\nfeat(tank-sim): milestone 1 — workspace skeleton, core types, RNG, save/load, and preset data\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_38\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"I’ve got the completed loop-1 artifacts now. The approved notes explicitly defer source-water chemistry mixing and heat-driven ambient response, which makes the next slice narrower than the original milestone name.\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
